HiDPI, world and interface scaled apart (follow-up to 0056, 0062, 0071).

0071 raised the whole canvas scale (2x from 1300 lines), so on a Retina or
ultrawide screen the world was magnified too: fewer cells, big soft sprites.
Now the interface (sidebar, text, menus) keeps its whole k screen pixels per
canvas pixel while the world is drawn at the screen's own pixels: the starting
tactical zoom is 1/k (zoom_start), so a bigger screen shows more map and sprites
are 1 art pixel on 1 screen pixel. SDL already gives the drawable size in pixels
(ALLOW_HIGHDPI, SDL_GetWindowSizeInPixels), so no change there.
- RA2_UI_SCALE=1..4 (launcher: Interface size) fixes k (never under 720 lines).
- RA2_WORLD_ZOOM=1..4 (launcher: World zoom, 1 = Automatic) multiplies native.
- zoom_min goes down to 1/k (0.25 at most), zoom_max lets units grow to k screen
  pixels (2 on a 1:1 screen); zoom > 1 now also goes through the world texture;
  a whole number of screen pixels per world pixel is drawn with nearest sampling.
- A canvas change (resize, monitor) returns to the start zoom unless the player
  zoomed; the start camera and the campaign pan use the world-view size.
- Dev: with RA2_AUTOSHOT_DIR the match writes game.png after 150 frames and ends.
Not tried on a real Mac: checked on Linux with Xvfb at 3440x1440, 5120x3200 and 1920x1080 windows.
